  "findings": [
    "PDS3 dataset page directly links the PDS4 collection. PDS4 collection modification date2026-06-20, individual product labels2026-06-23 and citation publication2026 are migration/publication metadata, not new observations.",
    "Both PDS4 FITS files independently fetched unchanged and exactly byte-equal to retained PDS3 originals, including headers, primary image, error/quality extensions and padding. No recompression, scaling or source replacement.",
    "Collection history explicitly says data unchanged while some PDS4 geometry attributes were recalculated with a newer SPICE kernel. Product geometry names nh_v07.tm. Byte-identical FITS does not establish equality of all label geometry or current pointing/physical registration.",
    "Product target Jupiter VII (Elara), times2007-03-05T11:00:01.330Z\u201301.370Z and11:00:02.330Z\u201302.370Z remain distinct. PDS4 Partially Processed primary image at byte37440 remains float32 calibrated DN, not independently reproduced radiance/I-F or calibrated visible colour.",
    "PDS3/PDS4 root and exact Elara data directories provide FITS/labels; no compact Elara JPEG/PNG browse product appears in these inspected listings. Dataset Browse link means directory navigation, not proof of a browse image. This is not an exhaustive search or global image-unavailability claim.",
    "Inspected NASA overview body provides text but no identified Elara-specific image. Generic page/footer images are not assigned to Elara. Secondary search leads were used only to locate the already retained primary PDS directory; no third-party rendered image downloaded/adopted.",
    "Published instrument FOV/pixel sampling in collection prose are retained publisher specifications only; no new angular/raster computation, target diameter or surface resolution inferred."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "PDS4 label schema validation, full collection inventory completeness, SPICE kernels/loading/geometry reproduction and mapping of each updated label field to PDS3 remain open. The two exact product LIDVIDs each occur once as primary members in the retained inventory; this does not validate every collection member.",
    "No newly independent target-centroid/PSF/shape/terrain identification or calibrated photometry/colour. Native unresolved imagery does not establish resolved local geography or chemistry.",
    "No official compact publisher rendition verified in inspected sources. A disclosed source-preserving display derivative would require its own processing/provenance assessment before adoption.",
    "Both independent imagined Elara views/masters/previews remain prepared; standalone capacity still needed before additive integration. All earlier science/rotation/thermal/spectral/registration limitations remain."
  ],
